<title>SRI LANKA: Lion opens sharply up on debut.</title>
<headline>Lion opens sharply up on debut.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lion Brewery Ltd, which began trading on Wednesday, opened 35 percent or seven rupees higher at 27, on turnover of 1,000 shares, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;With the beer market booming, the share is being focused on,&quot; said a local broker.</p>
<p>Beer sales have soared after the government slashed excise duty in late 1995. A further 43,000 Lion shares are on bid at 24.75 rupees.</p>
<p>Lion, a Ceylon Brewery subsidiary, made an initial offer of 12.5 million shares at 20 rupees, in November 1996. --Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
